13
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:12,970
So, what I'm trying to do
所以 我想做的是

14
00:01:12,970 --> 00:01:15,430
is create a metaphorical conversation
在

15
00:01:15,430 --> 00:01:17,930
between George Orwell and Jack Kerouac,
乔治·奥威尔和杰克·凯鲁亚克之间

16
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:20,190
as if Down and Out in Paris and London
展开一场隐喻性的对话

17
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:23,150
was typed out on one long piece of paper.
就好像《巴黎伦敦落魄
记》是用一张长纸打出来的

18
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:26,480
Snappy. Splenetic. High velocity.
干练 刻薄 节奏明快

19
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,320
At its core, it's a building's Roman,
它的核心

20
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:33,660
but not in the sad Salinger,
smoking, woman-hating way.
是一部成长小说 但不是那种悲伤的、
抽着烟的、厌女的塞林格风格

21
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,280
It's hopeful.
它是充满希望的

22
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,950
And I know I put it on my application,
我知道

23
00:01:36,950 --> 00:01:38,580
but in terms of timeline,
我在申请表里写了 不过就时间线而言

24
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:41,620
I'd want to have the first draft done by July.
我希望在七月份前完成初稿

25
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:44,710
Then submit for notes
from this esteemed troika,
然后交给这三位尊敬的大佬审阅并提意见

26
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:46,670
do a quick polish,
快速润色一下

27
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:48,340
and hopefully spend the rest of my summer
然后希望我剩下的夏天

28
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,840
in a state of "boketto."
都能处于“发呆”的状态

29
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,800
That's what the Japanese say
日本人就是这么说的

30
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,300
when you gaze out in the distance
当你眺望远方

31
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,720
